ingredients:
  - "1 cup buckwheat flour (kuttu ka atta)"
  - "1/2 cup yogurt"
  - "1/4 tsp cumin seeds"
  - "1 green chili, finely chopped"
  - "1/4 tsp turmeric powder"
  - "Salt to taste"
  - "Water (as required to adjust batter consistency)"
  - "1 tbsp oil for cooking"
instructions:
  - "In a mixing bowl, combine the buckwheat flour, yogurt, cumin seeds, chopped green chili, turmeric, and salt."
  - "Add water gradually to make a smooth batter with a consistency similar to pancake batter."
  - "Heat a non-stick pan and drizzle a little oil."
  - "Pour a ladle of batter onto the pan and spread it into a round shape."
  - "Cook on medium heat until both sides are golden brown."
  - "Serve hot with chutney or a dollop of yogurt."
